{"id": "EUVD-2026-80421", "enisaUuid": "6c50a3fb-7abc-361b-ac8f-ad658d71992e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: avoid divide-by-zero in __is_lut_linear()\n\n__is_lut_linear() computes the expected value of each entry with\n\n\texpected = i * MAX_DRM_LUT_VALUE / (size - 1);\n\nIf it is ever called with a single-entry LUT, size - 1 is zero and the\nkernel takes a divide error (#DE). A LUT with fewer than two entries\ncannot describe a linear mapping anyway, so return false early instead\nof dividing by zero.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:30:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:53:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2320626425f3af3a25b8afb6876f205b1c6d4e64", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d1e06d5dc8f12451ce71dc068342660a34476084", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c127ace7af2b40107947a6504391f94d6fd21734", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d5ee095a58461b2446d7a6eb0c14c2fe3eaab44", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5f18cd1ba873e751bf5547407ad44ea34adfbe2f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee28fafb50f58b847509b5240b431ddec673bdfe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/15ee43aad0df43dfd1dbb32e7d5b951745c4b87f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4f40873f8a4107df2b9c8e68c947c4fd0cd519d2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89821", "GHSA-4rrm-wvmv-qhx6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "047cdb04-92a1-3b1a-adad-3f1232cc3720", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "086247a4b2fba49800b27807f22bb894cd8363fb <ee28fafb50f58b847509b5240b431ddec673bdfe"}, {"id": "0ccb5464-ba14-38c3-8fda-95e9e4f367fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.17"}, {"id": "1af5eabf-c1fb-3970-b408-559f06d47114", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "086247a4b2fba49800b27807f22bb894cd8363fb <2320626425f3af3a25b8afb6876f205b1c6d4e64"}, {"id": "1dc7380c-2ea7-3794-b6